  - [[Page~131 (1)耕(1)畊 _(1)Kang_ (gang1); here normalised to _(1)K(a/)ng_ (gaang1)]]
    ==
    - To plough, to cultivate fields;
    - the period for ploughing;
    - a ploughing;
    - to labor, to be diligent in any occupation;
    - _~~(1)kang~~ ``(1)k(a/)ng`` (1)f(u/)_ [[gaang1 fu1]],
        or
      _~~(1)kang~~ ``(1)k(a/)ng`` (4)t(')(i/)n (4)yan_ [[gaang1 tin4 jan4]],
        a ploughman, a farmer, an agriculturist;
    - _muk(9) ~~(1)kang~~ ``(1)k(a/)ng``_
        [[muk6 gaang1]],
        to labor with the eyes for a living, as a physiognomist;
    - _sh(i/)t(8) ~~(1)kang~~ ``(1)k(a/)ng``_
        [[sit3 gaang1]],
        to teach for a living;
    - _lik(9) ~~(1)kang~~ ``(1)k(a/)ng``_
        [[lik6 gaang1]],
        to work hard at a business;
    - _~~(1)kang~~ ``(1)k(a/)ng`` (2)tsai_
        [[gaang1 zai2]],
        hired laborers on a farm;
    - _(1)hoi ~~(1)kang~~ ``(1)k(a/)ng``_
        [[hoi1 gaang1]],
        to begin ploughing.
    ==
  ====
